            <ArticleTitle>An audit of asthma care in minor injury units.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>457-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Asthma was found to be one of the commonest reasons for attendance at nurse-led minor injury units in Cornwall. Care provided in these units should comply with BTS guidelines and local protocols. Ongoing education must be provided to ensure staff maintain the recommended standards of care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
